WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.772
Hello, and welcome.

00:00:02.772 --> 00:00:04.982
This little film is just for you.

00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:13.217
It shows the next steps to open your shop for real, so customers can buy your treasures and the money arrives in your bank.

00:00:13.217 --> 00:00:15.292
You don't need to be technical.

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:17.837
Sit back, and pause whenever you like.

00:00:18.637 --> 00:00:20.159
Here is where we are.

00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:26.179
Your shop is built, and it is already on the internet at www dot sycapooke dot com.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:27.339
It looks lovely.

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:29.805
But right now it can't take money.

00:00:29.805 --> 00:00:38.725
Three things are still missing: your treasures, a payment account, and a few finishing touches from your technical partner.

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:41.589
There are five steps.

00:00:41.589 --> 00:00:45.704
One: get your treasures ready, with photos and a few notes.

00:00:45.704 --> 00:00:48.983
Two: open a Stripe account, so you can be paid.

00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:52.470
Three: your technical partner connects everything.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.330
Four: you put your treasures on the site.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.329
Five: you sell, you ship, and you get paid.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:02.932
Steps one and two are yours, and you can start them today.

00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:05.095
Step three is your partner's job.

00:01:05.095 --> 00:01:06.603
Let's go one at a time.

00:01:08.003 --> 00:01:11.150
Start with ten or twenty of your favourite pieces.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.416
Your phone's camera is all you need.

00:01:14.216 --> 00:01:18.360
Take photos in daylight, near a window, but out of strong sun.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:23.306
Lay the piece on a plain background, like a white sheet or a wooden table.

00:01:23.306 --> 00:01:25.111
Show the whole piece first.

00:01:25.111 --> 00:01:28.252
That first photo becomes the cover in the shop.

00:01:29.052 --> 00:01:32.251
Then take a few close ups. The maker's mark.

00:01:32.251 --> 00:01:33.923
The clasp or the label.

00:01:33.923 --> 00:01:35.740
Any little chips or wear.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.957
Honest photos build trust, and customers love the details.

00:01:39.957 --> 00:01:43.519
You can add up to eight photos for each treasure.

00:01:44.919 --> 00:01:47.715
Next, for each treasure, write a short note.

00:01:47.715 --> 00:01:49.114
A notebook is perfect.

00:01:49.114 --> 00:01:50.575
You'll need six things.

00:01:51.375 --> 00:01:53.812
A name, like gold filigree brooch.

00:01:53.812 --> 00:01:57.466
Its story: where it came from and why it's special.

00:01:57.466 --> 00:01:59.974
The maker or brand, if you know it.

00:01:59.974 --> 00:02:02.768
Its condition, such as used, excellent.

00:02:02.768 --> 00:02:06.996
A price, anywhere from one dollar to five thousand dollars.

00:02:06.996 --> 00:02:08.429
And a shipping cost.

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:13.660
You can choose free shipping, or a flat amount up to one hundred dollars.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.735
A tip for shipping.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:22.779
Pack one piece in its box, weigh it at the post office, and ask what it costs to send across the country.

00:02:22.779 --> 00:02:26.133
Use that as your shipping cost for similar pieces.

00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:28.768
Now, getting paid.

00:02:28.768 --> 00:02:36.449
Stripe is a well known company that takes your customers' card payments safely and sends the money to your bank.

00:02:36.449 --> 00:02:38.987
Card numbers never touch our website.

00:02:38.987 --> 00:02:41.113
Stripe looks after all of that.

00:02:41.913 --> 00:02:43.587
There's no monthly fee.

00:02:43.587 --> 00:02:52.538
As of November 2026, Stripe's standard rate for American cards is two point nine percent, plus thirty cents, for each sale.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:58.651
So on a one hundred dollar sale, you keep about ninety six dollars and eighty cents.

00:02:58.651 --> 00:03:01.854
Sycapooke itself takes no commission at all.

00:03:01.854 --> 00:03:07.166
Your partner can check stripe dot com slash pricing for the latest rates.

00:03:07.966 --> 00:03:10.450
Before you start, gather these things.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.803
Your email address and mobile phone.

00:03:12.803 --> 00:03:15.157
Your home address and date of birth.

00:03:15.157 --> 00:03:16.987
Your Social Security number.

00:03:16.987 --> 00:03:20.255
And your bank's routing number and account number.

00:03:20.255 --> 00:03:23.785
You'll find both at the bottom of one of your cheques.

00:03:24.585 --> 00:03:29.440
Then, on your computer, go to stripe dot com and press Start now.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:34.520
Enter your email, your name, and a password, and confirm your email.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.582
Stripe will then ask about your business.

00:03:37.582 --> 00:03:40.420
Choose individual, or sole proprietor.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.080
For the website, enter www dot sycapooke dot com.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:50.878
Describe what you sell: antiques and vintage jewelry, clothing, housewares and electronics.

00:03:50.878 --> 00:03:53.193
Finally, add your bank account.

00:03:53.193 --> 00:03:55.434
Stripe sends your money there.

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:59.786
Please turn on two step sign in when Stripe offers it.

00:03:59.786 --> 00:04:04.523
It sends a code to your phone, so nobody else can get into your account.

00:04:05.923 --> 00:04:08.158
Here's the most important part.

00:04:08.158 --> 00:04:12.627
Never send passwords or secret codes by email or text message.

00:04:12.627 --> 00:04:16.520
Instead, invite your partner into your Stripe account.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.908
Open Settings, then Team, and press Add member.

00:04:19.908 --> 00:04:25.603
Type your partner's email address, choose the Developer role, and press Invite.

00:04:26.403 --> 00:04:26.989
That's it.

00:04:26.989 --> 00:04:31.619
Your partner can then connect Stripe to the shop, without you copying anything.

00:04:31.619 --> 00:04:32.967
And you stay the owner.

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:37.323
While you take photos, your partner has four jobs.

00:04:37.323 --> 00:04:42.881
You don't need to do these, but it helps to know about them, so you can ask how they're going.

00:04:43.681 --> 00:04:48.786
First, connect Stripe to the shop, so the checkout can take real payments.

00:04:48.786 --> 00:04:50.787
Second, switch on real email.

00:04:50.787 --> 00:04:54.098
Today, the shop's emails don't reach anyone yet.

00:04:54.098 --> 00:04:59.963
Customers need them to confirm their accounts, and you need them to hear about sales.

00:04:59.963 --> 00:05:02.239
Third, make you the shop's owner.

00:05:02.239 --> 00:05:09.553
And fourth, do a real test: buy something small, then refund it, to be sure the money flows the right way.

00:05:10.353 --> 00:05:11.746
A word on sales tax.

00:05:11.746 --> 00:05:15.926
Ask an accountant whether you must collect it in your state.

00:05:15.926 --> 00:05:22.266
If you do, Stripe has a tool for it that your partner can switch on, for a small extra fee.

00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:24.930
Now the fun part.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:29.314
On your computer or phone, go to app dot sycapooke dot com.

00:05:29.314 --> 00:05:32.584
Press Join. Enter your email and a password.

00:05:32.584 --> 00:05:37.713
Then open the email from Sycapooke, and press the link to confirm it.

00:05:38.513 --> 00:05:40.370
Tell your partner you've joined.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:45.651
Once they make you the owner, you'll see a new button at the top of the page: Sell an item.

00:05:46.451 --> 00:05:49.520
Press Sell an item. First, add your photos.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.874
Press Add photos and choose them from your phone or computer.

00:05:53.874 --> 00:05:55.801
The first one is the cover.

00:05:55.801 --> 00:06:01.155
Then pick the category, like jewelry, and the type, like brooches and pins.

00:06:01.155 --> 00:06:03.082
The size is always vintage.

00:06:03.082 --> 00:06:05.294
The shop fills that in for you.

00:06:06.094 --> 00:06:13.073
Next, copy in your note card: the name, the story, the maker, the condition, the price, and the shipping cost.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:16.603
When everything looks right, press Publish.

00:06:16.603 --> 00:06:19.334
Your treasure is in the shop straight away.

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:20.160
Not finished?

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.954
Press Save draft, and come back to it later.

00:06:22.954 --> 00:06:25.812
You can publish up to twenty treasures a day.

00:06:26.612 --> 00:06:32.255
To change a price later, or take a piece down, open Inventory at the top of the page.

00:06:33.655 --> 00:06:40.720
When someone buys a treasure, Stripe takes their payment, and the piece is marked sold, so nobody else can buy it.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.129
You'll get an email, and the order appears under Sales.

00:06:44.929 --> 00:06:45.896
Open the order.

00:06:45.896 --> 00:06:49.573
It shows the customer's address, and the date to ship by.

00:06:49.573 --> 00:06:51.378
You have five business days.

00:06:51.378 --> 00:07:00.343
If a piece isn't shipped in time, the order is cancelled and the customer gets their money back automatically, so please keep an eye on it.

00:07:01.143 --> 00:07:04.927
Pack the treasure with care and take it to the post office.

00:07:04.927 --> 00:07:07.621
Keep the receipt with the tracking number.

00:07:07.621 --> 00:07:15.765
Then open the order, press Add tracking, choose the carrier, such as USPS, type the tracking number, and press Mark as shipped.

00:07:15.765 --> 00:07:18.843
The customer is sent the tracking link by email.

00:07:19.643 --> 00:07:20.517
And the money?

00:07:20.517 --> 00:07:25.447
Stripe sends it to your bank automatically, usually within a few business days.

00:07:25.447 --> 00:07:31.063
You can see every payment in Stripe, on your computer, or in the Stripe app on your phone.

00:07:31.863 --> 00:07:35.564
If a customer has a problem, it appears under Support.

00:07:35.564 --> 00:07:42.830
You read what they say, then choose: give a full refund, or close it without one, with a kind explanation.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:48.114
Once your first treasures are in the shop, share it.

00:07:48.114 --> 00:07:50.279
Tell your friends and family.

00:07:50.279 --> 00:07:58.195
Post photos of your favourite pieces on Facebook or Instagram, with the address www dot sycapooke dot com.

00:07:58.195 --> 00:08:02.451
Every treasure has a story, and people love to hear them.

00:08:03.851 --> 00:08:06.107
So, here is your list for this week.

00:08:06.107 --> 00:08:09.617
Photograph ten treasures and write a note card for each.

00:08:09.617 --> 00:08:13.691
Open your Stripe account, and invite your partner as a Developer.

00:08:13.691 --> 00:08:19.144
Then, when your partner says it's ready, join the shop and publish your first treasure.

00:08:19.944 --> 00:08:21.726
You've built something beautiful.

00:08:21.726 --> 00:08:24.049
Now let's share it. Thank you for watching.
